<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tokugawa Nariaki</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1800–1860</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tokugawa Nariaki (1800–1860) was the ninth lord of the Mito domain from 1829 and a leading advocate of coastal defence and the expulsion of foreigners. He founded the Kōdōkan school and promoted the Mito school's loyalty to the emperor. He opposed the treaties with Western powers, was confined by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ii-naosuke">Ii Naosuke</a> in the Ansei purge, and was the father of the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-yoshinobu">Tokugawa Yoshinobu</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tokugawa-nariaki.jpg" alt="Tokugawa Nariaki" width="320" height="377" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknow author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%BE%B3%E5%B7%9D%E6%96%89%E6%98%AD%E8%82%96%E5%83%8F(2).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
